        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5af5a5aa-e52e-5601-9871-5c21060fb4a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Crab fisheries, crustacean harvest, seafood\n- Species: True crabs, horse crab (Portunus trituberculatus), Dungeness crab (Metacarcinus magister/Cancer magister), rock crab, shrimp\n- Organizations: WoRMS, ITIS\n- Places: West coast of North America, Deer Harbor, Washington\n\nFacts:\n- Crab fisheries capture or farm crabs.\n- True crabs make up 20% of all crustaceans caught and farmed worldwide, and about 1.4 million tonnes are consumed annually.\n- The horse crab, Portunus trituberculatus, accounts for one quarter of the total true-crab consumption or harvest amount.\n- WoRMS recognizes the Dungeness crab as Metacarcinus magister, while ITIS recognizes it as Cancer magister.\n- The Dungeness crab inhabits eelgrass beds and water bottoms on the west coast of North America.\n- The Dungeness crab typically grows to 20 cm across the carapace and is a popular seafood valued for its sweet, tender flesh.\n- In Deer Harbor, Washington, many people fish for Dungeness crab, rock crab, and shrimp.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c35b2115-748b-5e60-a227-0c966447fed9",
        "text": "Page: Crab fisheries. Sentence: Crab fisheries are fisheries which capture or farm crabs. True crabs make up 20% of all crustaceans caught and farmed worldwide, with about 1.4 million tonnes being consumed annually.\nPage: Crab fisheries. Sentence: The horse crab, \"Portunus trituberculatus\" accounts for one quarter of that total.\nPage: Dungeness crab. Sentence: The Dungeness crab, Metacarcinus magister (the naming convention recognized by WoRMS) or Cancer magister (the naming convention recognized by ITIS), is a species of crab that inhabits eelgrass beds and water bottoms on the west coast of North America.\nPage: Dungeness crab. Sentence: It typically grows to 20 cm across the carapace and is a popular seafood prized for its sweet and tender flesh.\nPage: Deer Harbor, Washington. Sentence: Many people fish for Dungeness crab, rock crab, and shrimp there.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
